---
import ContentSection from "~/components/content-section.astro";
---

<ContentSection title="Required setup" id="setup">
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    Camera, ArUco markers, and optionally a FluidNC controller.
  </Fragment>
  <div class="w-full max-w-3xl text-base text-offset">
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-4 pl-5 text-left">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-default">Camera:</strong> Mounted so it has a clear view of the CNC table. Options include:
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 mt-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Old smartphone</strong> -
            <a href="https://makerworld.com/en/models/1455114-ceiling-top-down-phone-mount-with-ball-joint#profileId-1516416"
               class="text-primary hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Ceiling mount 3D print model
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>IP camera</strong> - Requires
            <a href="https://github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc"
               class="text-primary hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              go2rtc
            </a> gateway to expose stream in a compatible way. Go2rtc can run on a Raspberry Pi Zero or any local machine.
            <a href="https://makerworld.com/en/models/1461605-reolink-e1-zoom-ceiling-down-mount-looking-down#profileId-1524062"
               class="text-primary hover:underline ml-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Reolink E1 Zoom 3D print model
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
        Camera calibration is integrated as part of the setup process.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-default">Markers:</strong> Printed ArUco markers keep pose estimation locked in, even if the camera or wasteboard moves.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-default">(Optional) CNC controller:</strong>
        <a href="http://wiki.fluidnc.com/en/features/webui"
           class="text-primary hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          FluidNC WebUI v3
        </a> integration for click-to-jog and sending programs directly. Does not work offline ATM, so FluidNC needs to run in STA mode.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</ContentSection>
